1. The finding and its rule

  F1 [blocker] of `measure/runs/model_guide/check-4.9.json`. The one-pass
  guard of `review-run.sh` keyed on an empty `QUOTA_PROVIDER`. The committed
  no-source rows set a provider (`nvidia`) and a null `quota_source`, so the
  guard never fired and a second pass of the same date ran.

  The Red test e60814a states the contract. The guard keys on an empty or
  null `quota_source`. A second run of a no-source route for the same
  `--date` exits 2 before any call. It prints exactly one stderr line that
  starts `review-run:` and holds `one pass per night`. Its stdout is empty.
  It starts no job and writes no second pass record.

2. Base evidence

  At the role base e60814a, `review-run.test.ts` ran with
  `Tests  1 failed | 24 passed (25)`. The failure was F1: the second run
  exited 0 instead of 2. The F2 case passed at the base.

3. Change

  `harness/model-guide/review-run.sh` keys the guard on
  `[ -z "$QUOTA_SOURCE" ]`. The refusal prints one line on stderr and exits
  2, the same shape as the lock refusal. The guard still runs after the
  slug and tag are known and before the quota read and any call. The script
  header names the rule.

  No other change. No test file changed.

